// Adding and modifying properties is fun and easy!  Here's how you can do it:
// Each property that you want to show up in the properies list in the editor
// will follow this basic format:
//
// Properties	{
//	Name	"PropertyName"
//	Type	theType
// }
//
// "PropertyName" is the name of the property you're adding
// theType is one of the following types:
//   TextBox:	Lets the user enter any string
//   Slider:	Gives the user a slider to enter the value (as well as a text box if necessary)
//   IntegerSlider: Same as Slider, but restricts values to integer values
//   RadioButtons:  Shows a list of buttons to select possible values from
//   ComboBox:	  Like RadioButtons, but the strings are in a combo box instead
//
// If you chose TextBox, you're done
// If you chose a slider of some kind, you must specify the min and max values of the slider
//
// Properties	{
//	Name	"Foo"
//	Type	Slider
//	Min	10
//	Max	100
// }
//
// If you chose RadioButtons or ComboBox, you must specify the possible values for those properties
//
// Properties	{
//	Name	"Bar"
//	Type	RadioButtons
//	Strings "Wing","Ding","Foobar"
// }
//
// That's it!

